  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/70EC23">Remark <span data-tag="70EC23">2.4.1.4</span>.</a> Let $p: X \rightarrow S$ be an inner fibration of simplicial sets. Unwinding the definition, we see that an edge $f: \Delta ^1 \rightarrow X$ is $p$-Cartesian if and only if for every $n \geq 2$ and every commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \Delta ^{ \{ n-1, n\}  } \ar [dr]^{f} \ar @{^{(}->}[d] &amp;  \\ \Lambda ^ n_ n \ar [r] \ar @{^{(}->}[d] &amp;  X \ar [d]^{p} \\ \Delta ^ n \ar [r] \ar @{-->}[ur] &amp;  S, } \]
</div>
  <p> there exists a dotted arrow as indicated, rendering the diagram commutative. </p>
